From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0337-frizti-07-small-uniforms-compared-in-place.patch

Source: 0337-frizti-07-small-uniforms-compared-in-place.patch
buffer_cache: compare small uniform buffers in guest memory (off by default)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Applies on core16 alone.

Source: Frizti/Lichii b44f87ad3d (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166), GPL-3.0-or-later.

EDEN_NX2_UBO_INPLACE=1. Each small uniform bind copies the buffer to a scratch area, compares it with
the slot, then copies it twice more if it changed. With the switch it compares in guest memory:
nothing is copied when the bytes are the same in the same command buffer, and the stream copy always
comes from the slot, so the two never differ even if the guest writes meanwhile.

Changed from the source: no counters.

Runs on the PS5: yes, on the back, unless EDEN_NX2_UBOREUSE=0.
Hang: no wait added. Pool memory: none.
Checked: 4 million random binds in place and 2 million without GetSpan, through this header with a
mock runtime, under ASan and UBSan: the bound bytes always equal guest memory, 680,000 of them reused.
PS5-target syntax compile. Not run.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/uniform_stream_reuse.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/uniform_stream_reuse.h
index 7ba31c4717..ed85de1d4e 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/uniform_stream_reuse.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/uniform_stream_reuse.h
@@ -40,6 +40,19 @@ concept StreamUniformReusable = requires(R& runtime, u32 size) {
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_NX2_UBO_INPLACE=1: BindSmallUniformReusing compares a buffer whose device pages are one
+/// host run (always so within one 4 KiB page) with its slot's bytes in guest memory, instead of
+/// copying it to a scratch buffer first. Unchanged bytes are then not copied at all, changed ones
+/// are copied once to the slot and the stream copy is made from the slot, so the two never differ,
+/// as the scratch snapshot made sure. From Frizti/Lichii b44f87ad3d (Dr. Sergio, Lichii PR 166).
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool UniformInPlaceCompareEnabled() noexcept {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_UBO_INPLACE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 template <class Ref>
 class UniformStreamReuse {
 public:
@@ -97,6 +110,27 @@ template <class Runtime, class DeviceMemory>
     }
     Reuse& reuse = UniformStreamReuseState<typename Runtime::StreamUniformRef>();
     typename Reuse::Slot& slot = reuse.slots[stage][index];
+    // Test memories have no GetSpan.
+    if constexpr (requires { device_memory.GetSpan(device_addr, size); }) {
+        const u8* const guest =
+            UniformInPlaceCompareEnabled() ? device_memory.GetSpan(device_addr, size) : nullptr;
+        if (guest != nullptr) {
+            const bool same = slot.size == size && std::memcmp(slot.bytes.data(), guest, size) == 0;
+            if (same && slot.tick == runtime.CurrentTick()) {
+                runtime.RebindStreamUniform(slot.ref, size);
+                return true;
+            }
+            if (!same) {
+                std::memcpy(slot.bytes.data(), guest, size);
+                slot.size = size;
+            }
+            const std::span<u8> span = runtime.BindMappedUniformBuffer(stage, binding_index, size);
+            std::memcpy(span.data(), slot.bytes.data(), size);
+            slot.ref = runtime.LastStreamUniformRef();
+            slot.tick = runtime.CurrentTick();
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
     u8* const scratch = reuse.scratch.data();
     device_memory.ReadBlockUnsafe(device_addr, scratch, size);
 
